  "answer_text": "AUTHENTICATION_FAILED for an IPsec tunnel is usually caused by a PSK mismatch between peers. The PSK must match exactly on both sides and the auth payloads must align; you can check this by reviewing the site IPsec connection history for payload mismatches and by capturing IKE traffic with a PCAP. PSKs are supported up to 64 characters, so ensure your PSK length meets the requirements. For troubleshooting, use the IPSec site connectivity troubleshooting guide and the built-in tools in the Cato Management Application (Timeline, PCAP, Connection Status) to identify configuration mismatches.",
